diff --git a/docs/ops/logging.md b/docs/ops/logging.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..76fec34
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/ops/logging.md
@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+# Logging lanes
+
+PegaFila splits observability into three lanes. Pick the one that matches the
+situation; do not mix them.
+
+## Archive — `daily` (default stack)
+
+- Driver: `daily`, file `storage/logs/laravel.log`, 14-day retention.
+- Level: `LOG_LEVEL` (default `debug`).
+- Use for routine application logs: debug/info/warning/error output produced by
+  the framework and by `Log::debug|info|warning|error(...)`.
+- Rotated daily; nothing is shipped externally.
+
+## Audit — `audit`
+
+- Driver: `daily`, file `storage/logs/audit.log`, level `LOG_AUDIT_LEVEL`
+  (default `info`), 90-day retention.
+- Use for a durable "who changed what / who tried what" trail: membership role
+  changes, subscription transitions, login lockouts, permission denials that
+  matter for forensics.
+- Write explicitly: `Log::channel('audit')->info('Subscription status changed', [...])`.
+- Do not use for routine debugging; do not put secrets/PII beyond what the
+  audit trail requires.
+
+## Alert — `App\Ops\DiscordOpsAlert`
+
+- Discord is **not** a Monolog channel. It is an explicit call made by code that
+  decides an incident is worth waking someone up for.
+- Use for actionable production incidents: a job that exhausted its retries, a
+  payment-gateway webhook failing, a plan limit blocking an entity.
+- API: `app(DiscordOpsAlert::class)->send($title, $message, $context)`.
+- When `DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL` is unset/empty the call is a silent no-op.
+- Never log or expose the webhook URL (it embeds the webhook token).
+
+## Decision guide
+
+- "Should I record this for later debugging?" → Archive (`Log::...`).
+- "Should we be able to prove who did what?" → Audit (`Log::channel('audit')`).
+- "Does someone need to act on this now?" → Alert (`DiscordOpsAlert::send`).
+- When in doubt, start with Archive; escalate to Audit for security-relevant
+  actions and to Alert only for actionable breakage.
